+// S6 SPIKE DRAFT — @workspec/canvas re-adoption shim (#122).
+//
+// This file REPLACES the 704-line enterprise store with a compatibility
+// shim over the package's store factory. Design goal: the 18 external
+// import sites (`import { useCanvasStore } from '@/canvas/store'`) keep
+// working UNMODIFIED in all three access forms they use today:
+//
+//   1. `useCanvasStore(selector)` / `useCanvasStore()`   — reactive hook
+//   2. `useCanvasStore.getState()` / `.setState()`        — imperative
+//   3. `useCanvasStore.subscribe(listener)`               — subscription
+//
+// The trick: the enterprise app is a ONE-CANVAS-PER-PAGE app (the module
+// singleton was load-bearing, shared across ProjectGraphCanvas and every
+// standalone page). So the shim keeps a module-level singleton INSTANCE
+// and binds the hook to it directly with zustand's `useStore` — NOT the
+// package's context hook. `<CanvasProvider store={canvasInstance}>` is
+// still required around every `<Canvas>` mount (the package's own
+// components resolve the instance via context), but external panels that
+// only read the store need no provider — exactly today's semantics.
+//
